# WorkLedger — Arquivos gerados: Dockerfiles, Makefile, CI/CD e helpers

Abaixo estão os arquivos prontos para colar no repositório. Copia/cola para os caminhos indicados. Se quiser, eu ajusto nomes/paths conforme o teu repo.

---

## `docker-compose.yml`

```yaml
version: '3.9'

services:
  api:
    build:
      context: ./apps/api
      dockerfile: Dockerfile
    container_name: workledger-api
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "8000:8000"
    volumes:
      - ./apps/api:/var/www/html
      - ./packages:/var/www/packages
    environment:
      - APP_ENV=local
      - APP_DEBUG=true
    depends_on:
      - db
    networks:
      - workledger

  web:
    build:
      context: ./apps/web
      dockerfile: Dockerfile
    container_name: workledger-web
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "5173:5173"
    stdin_open: true
    tty: true
    volumes:
      - ./apps/web:/app
    depends_on:
      - api
    networks:
      - workledger

  db:
    image: mysql:8.0
    container_name: workledger-db
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "3307:3306" # host:container
    environment:
      MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: root
      MYSQL_DATABASE: workledger
      MYSQL_USER: workledger
      MYSQL_PASSWORD: secret
    volumes:
      - ./infra/db/data:/var/lib/mysql
    networks:
      - workledger

networks:
  workledger:
    driver: bridge
```

---

## `apps/api/Dockerfile` (Laravel 12 + PHP 8.2)

```dockerfile
# base image
FROM php:8.2-fpm

# system deps
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
    git \
    unzip \
    libzip-dev \
    zip \
    libpng-dev \
    libonig-dev \
    libxml2-dev \
    default-mysql-client \
    curl \
  && docker-php-ext-install pdo_mysql mbstring exif pcntl bcmath gd zip

# composer
COPY --from=composer:2.6 /usr/bin/composer /usr/bin/composer

# workdir
WORKDIR /var/www/html

# copy and install
COPY . /var/www/html

RUN composer install --no-interaction --no-scripts --prefer-dist --no-progress --optimize-autoloader || true

# dev env: ensure storage and cache perms
RUN chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/html/storage /var/www/html/bootstrap/cache || true

# expose port for php artisan serve (we map 8000 -> 8000 in compose)
EXPOSE 8000

# default command — use artisan serve for dev convenience
CMD ["php", "artisan", "serve", "--host=0.0.0.0", "--port=8000"]
```

> Observação: para produção, constrói uma imagem mais segura (nginx + php-fpm) e não uses `artisan serve`.

